# Shell scripts run on Linux (CI, servers, and the POSIX installer) and must
# keep LF line endings even when the repository is checked out on Windows.
# Without this, a Windows checkout turns them into CRLF and `set -euo pipefail`
# fails with "invalid option name"; `make rebuild` then cannot run.
#
# Only the files that are executed by a POSIX shell are pinned. Pinning every
# source type would fight core.autocrlf on Windows checkouts and report hundreds
# of files as modified even though their content is unchanged.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts are Windows-only; keep a native CRLF checkout.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
